{"content":[{"c":["TARSHISH (P",{"c":["erson"],"sourceClass":"lc","t":"span"},")"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["1. One of Javan’s four sons and a descendant of Noah through Japheth’s line (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.1.7","r":"1Chr.1.7","rawR":"1Chr.1.7","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.1.7","value":"1Chr.1.7"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 1:7"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["2. Sixth of Bilhan’s seven sons. He was a capable leader in Benjamin’s tribe and numbered among those able to go to war (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.7.10","r":"1Chr.7.10","rawR":"1Chr.7.10","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.7.10","value":"1Chr.7.10"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 7:10"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["3. One of the seven princes of Persia and Media. These men had personal access to King Ahasuerus’s presence and positions of honor second only to the king himself (",{"href":"?bref=Esth.1.14","r":"Esth.1.14","rawR":"Esth.1.14","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Esth.1.14","value":"Esth.1.14"}],"t":"ref","v":"Est 1:14"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"TarshishPerson","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"1 Chr 1:7","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.1.7","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.1.7","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.1.7"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 7:10","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.7.10","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.7.10","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.7.10"},{"anchorText":"Est 1:14","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Esth.1.14","rawQueryValue":"Esth.1.14","sourceRefExact":"Esth.1.14"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"41014546757f4a83437d0d0a33f451694f11cdb380614a7f5d574ce537e2b9d2","sourceItemName":"TarshishPerson","sourceItemOrder":57,"sourceMember":"Articles/T.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttribu